"""Per-repository template for tools/build_notebook.py (NOTEBOOK_SPEC 2.2 §4 standalone carrier).

Only the task-specific prose and stage cells live here. Runtime install, the embedded package (three modules,
carried verbatim in dependency order), and the model pin/stage/verify cells are produced by the generator from
repository sources so they cannot drift from the package.

This template configures an E2E handwritten-text-line adaptation workflow: the pinned stepfun-ai/GOT-OCR-2.0-hf
snapshot is digest-verified and loaded, 800 MIT-licensed Belfort handwritten line images with their transcripts are
fetched as eight digest-pinned parquet row groups over HTTPS range requests, the records are validated and split by
line image, a synthetic printed page is recognised through the inference contract, the frozen model's character and
word error rates over the held-out lines are measured beside an empty-string and a constant-transcript baseline, a
bounded fine-tuning of the last four decoder layers runs on cached frozen-prefix hidden states with validation-CER
epoch selection, the held-out split is scored again, six held-out lines and the printed page are re-read with the
adapted model, and the adapter is exported and reloaded.

Review fixes (Notebook Review Framework v1, review PR #9, GOT-M1..M5 / GOT-m1..m4): the runtime is the fleet's uv
isolated environment (no in-kernel install, no restart); the guided layer (audience, task contract, how to use,
roadmap, predictions, worked answers, a change-one-thing activity, troubleshooting, glossary, conclusion) is added and
the setup cells are labelled Infrastructure; the split is described as what it is - a line-image split of one
collection with no page field - and Sections 4 and 8 report the transcripts repeated between splits and the held-out
rates without them (the same split as the Florence-2 sibling row); Section 8 answers the CER and the WER question
separately against each baseline and records the outcome instead of asserting a gain; Sections 5-7 start from the
pretrained model on every re-run and `adapt` refuses an adapted pipeline; BYOD states and checks its real minimum
(12 distinct images), names the split it refuses, reports dropped duplicates, refuses duplicate file names, takes a
path as well as an upload and explains a cancelled upload; the validation curve's rise after the kept epoch, the test
split size and the run-to-run spread are stated; and every experiment names its form field and rerun scope.
"""
