        "## Glossary\n\n"
        "- **Image tokens:** the 256 vectors the vision encoder hands the decoder for one image; the decoder reads them as if "
        "they were words of the prompt.\n"
        "- **Greedy decoding / stop string:** at every step the single most likely next token is taken; generation ends at "
        "the stop token `<|im_end|>` or at the token budget (then `truncated` is true).\n"
        "- **Levenshtein distance:** the minimum number of character (or word) insertions, deletions and substitutions that "
        "turn one string into another.\n"
        "- **CER / WER (micro):** total character (word) edits over total reference characters (words) across the split; "
        "**macro** is the mean of the per-line rates. Not capped at 1.0. A word is wrong if any of its characters is.\n"
        "- **Empty / constant-transcript baseline:** systems that never look at the image — predicting nothing, or one "
        "training transcript (the **medoid**, the line closest on average to the others) for every line.\n"
        "- **Causal language-model loss:** the cross-entropy of predicting each transcript token from the tokens before it; "
        "the prompt and image tokens are masked out.\n"
        "- **Frozen-prefix cache:** the hidden states after the frozen first twenty decoder layers for each training line, "
        "computed once without gradients and reused every epoch because nothing before them is trained.\n"
        "- **Epoch / validation selection / overfitting:** one pass over the training lines; the epoch kept is the one with "
        "the lowest validation CER (epoch 0 = the frozen model); overfitting is the training loss falling while the "
        "validation error rises.\n"
